---
description: Rules for modifying and creating new pages in the app
globs: astro-app/src/pages/**/*.astro
alwaysApply: false
---
[astro.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/astro.mdc)

- All pages live in `astro-app/src/pages/`
- Use Astro's `Layout` component from `@/layouts/Layout.astro` for consistent page structure
- Fallback components can be set by using `slot='fallback'` on a child component. The actual component does not need to support children, as this is a feature of AstroJS
- For server-side data fetching, use `Astro.callAction()` with actions from `astro:actions` (e.g., `Astro.callAction(actions.users.getUserProfile, { username })`)
- Handle errors gracefully when calling actions (check for `error` property in response)
- Use `Astro.locals` for accessing authenticated user state and other request context
- API routes should be placed in `astro-app/src/pages/api/` directory